#title Bard's Song (In the Forest)
#author Blind Guardian
#category Piosenki zagraniczne

#verse
Now you all know ~ a G
The bards and their songs ~ e7 a
When hours have gone by ~ a G
I'll close my eyes ~ e7 a
In a world far away ~ a G
We may meet again ~ e7 a
But now hear my song ~ a G
About the dawn of the night ~ e7 a
Let's sing the bards' song ~ C G a G

#chorus
Tomorrow will take us away ~ d a d a
Far from home ~ d a
No one will ever know our names ~ d F G d
But the bards' songs will remain ~ a G a
Tomorrow will take it away ~ d a d a
The fear of today ~ d a
It will be gone ~ d F
Due to our magic songs ~ C G e

#verse
 ~ a G e7 a

#verse
There's only one song ~ a G
Left in my mind ~ e7 a
Tales of a brave man ~ a G
Who lived far from here ~ e7 a
Now the bard songs are over ~ a G
And it's time to leave ~ e7 a
No one should ask you for the name ~ a G
Of the one ~ e7 a
Who tells the story ~ C G a G

#chorus
Tomorrow will take us away ~ d a d a
Far from home ~ d a
No one will ever know our names ~ d F G d
But the bards' songs will remain ~ a G a
Tomorrow all will be known ~ d a d a
And you're not alone ~ d a
So don't be afraid ~ d F
In the dark and cold ~ G d
'Cause the bards' songs will remain ~ a G C G a
They all will remain ~ C G a

#verse
In my thoughts and in my dreams ~ C G a
They're always in my mind ~ C G a
These songs of hobbits, dwarfs and men ~ C G a
And elves ~ C
Come close your eyes ~ G a
You can see them too ~ C G e7


